id: pm-gh1535
title: "GH-1535: report context test health over the matching population"
description: "Reproduce GH-1535: tests counters use the focus page while summary uses matching_items. Compute test health over the same filtered active population independently of focus limits. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1535"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:30:10.816Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:19.777Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:18.740Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:18.740Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Test counters are invariant under focus limits; Filters and active statuses constrain the denominator; Public SDK and human output declare test scope and denominator
parent: pm-gh1361
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "Count the complete matching active population and expose scope and denominator, while limiting Markdown failing identities by focus amount and native token cost and disclosing items_failing_omitted."
expected_result: Structured counts stay exact across focus limits and Markdown emits bounded failure detail with an explicit omitted count.
actual_result: "All48 linked context cases pass. SDK CLI and MCP counts agree across limits1/10; real Markdown at limit1 emits one of three failing IDs and omitted2, while a one-token detail budget emits no IDs and omitted3. Typecheck lint SDK surface and documentation checks pass. Hosted coverage and review remain merge prerequisites."
